      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "If $|Z|=1$ then $|P(P(P(Z)))|=$",
      "worked_solution": "For any set $S$, we have $|P(S)|={2}^{|S|}.$ \n\nIn our case, we have $|Z|=1.$ Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n|P(Z)|={2}^{1}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(P(Z))| & ={2}^{|P(Z)|} \\\\  & ={2}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(P(P(Z)))| & ={2}^{|P(P(Z))|} \\\\  & ={2}^{4} \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
